    "docid": "22490",
    "score": 17.844780629135315,
    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Every Question You Have About Kelly Ripa's Husband and Three Kids, Answered\ndate: 2024-06-27\n---\n- Kelly Ripa married Riverdale actor Mark Consuelos in May 1996.\n\n- The couple has three children: Michael, 27; Lola, 23; and Joaquin, 21.\n\n- In 2024, the couple celebrated 28 years of marriage.\n\nAfter almost three decades of marriage, Live With Kelly and Mark co-hosts Kelly Ripa and Mark Consuelos have solidified themselves as one of Hollywood's \"it\" couples. The duo have been together since they were in their 20s, and their love affair shows no signs of slowing down. Here's everything you need to know about their whirlwind romance, their rock-solid marriage and their three children.\n\nFebruary 1995: Kelly and Mark meet on the set of All My Children.\n\nIn 1990, Kelly was cast in her first major acting role as Hayley in the soap opera All My Children. Fast forward five years and Mark landed the part of Mateo Santos, Hayley's husband. It didn't take long for Mark to fall in love with his on-screen wife. Kelly however, says she knew he was the one before the two even met in person.\n\n\"I saw my husband in a photograph before I saw him [in real life],\" she told Radio Andy host Bruce Bozzi when interviewed in 2018. \"I knew when I saw his photograph.\"\n\nMay 1996: Mark and Kelly elope to Las Vegas.\n\nA little over a year after their first meeting, the two tied the knot. Following a brief breakup, Kelly and Mark got back together and immediately eloped in Las Vegas, saying \"I do\" on May 1, 1996. Kelly reportedly wore a $200 dress to the ceremony.\n\n\"I didn't buy it as a wedding dress. I just bought it because it was really pretty, and I wanted to buy something from the Barney's Warehouse sale,\" she said on Live! in April 2016.\n\nJune 1997: Kelly gives birth to their first child.\n\nThe couple's oldest son, Michael Joseph was born on June 2, 1997. Michael, now 27, is the spitting image of his father. So much so that he played the younger version of Mark's character, Hiram Lodge, on the popular CW drama Riverdale.\n\nJune 2001: Daughter Lola Grace is born.\n\n"
