    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Halle Bailey\ndate: 2024-01-26\n---\n2000-present\n\nLatest News: Halle Bailey Discusses the Birth of Her Son, Halo\n\nHalle Bailey spoke publicly for the first time about the December 2023 birth of her son, Halo, explaining that she decided to keep her pregnancy a secret to ensure a \"beautiful, private, healthy time in my journey.\" The 23-year-old and her boyfriend, rapper DDG, repeatedly dodged speculation about a possible pregnancy, though The Little Mermaid star was very much aware some fans had figured out the truth. She finally ended the suspense with an Instagram post on January 6 announcing Halo's birth.\n\nIn addition to her growing family, the singer and actor has had plenty to celebrate of late. Her latest movie The Color Purple hit theaters on Christmas Day, and she is also nominated for a 2024 Grammy Award for Best R&B Song for \"Angel.\" The track was released in August ahead of her debut solo album that's currently in the works.\n\nWho Is Halle Bailey?\n\nHalle Bailey is a singer and actor known as one half of the singing duo Chloe x Halle, along with her sister Chl\u00f6e Bailey. The pair rose to prominence after posting music videos on YouTube and winning the Radio Disney singing competition Next Big Thing. They have been nominated for five Grammy Awards, including Best Urban Contemporary Album for 2018's The Kids Are Alright and Best Progressive R&B Album for 2020's Ungodly Hour. Halle also received a 2024 nomination for her solo song \"Angel.\" In addition to her singing career, Halle is a rising actor whose roles have included Sky Forster in the TV show Grown-ish, Ariel in Disney's live-action movie The Little Mermaid, and a supporting part in 2023's The Color Purple, based on the 1982 novel by Alice Walker.\n\nQuick Facts\n\nFULL NAME: Halle Lynn Bailey\n\nBORN: March 27, 2000\n\nBIRTHPLACE: Atlanta, Georgia\n\nSIBLINGS: Ski, Chl\u00f6e Bailey, and Branson\n\nCHILD: Halo\n\nASTROLOGICAL SIGN: Aries\n\nEarly Life, Parents, and Siblings\n\nHalle Lynn Bailey was born on March 27, 2000, in Atlanta. She was raised in nearby Mableton by parents Courtney and Doug Bailey. Halle has three siblings: older sisters Ski and Chl\u00f6e, as well as younger"
