    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Kris Kristofferson's 8 Children: All About the Late Country Singer's Sons and Daughters\nauthor: Emily Weaver\ndate: 2025-05-22\n---\nKris Kristofferson was surrounded by a lot of love \u2014 and talent! \u2014 during his life thanks to his eight kids: Tracy, Kris Jr., Casey, Jesse, Jody, Johnny, Kelly Marie and Blake.\n\nThe beloved singer-songwriter, who died \"peacefully\" at home on Sept. 28 at age 88, shared daughter Tracy and son Kris Jr. with his former high school sweetheart, Frances Beer. Following their divorce, Kris fell in love with singer Rita Coolidge. During their seven-year marriage, they welcomed a daughter named Casey. In 1983, Kris married celebrity hairstylist Lisa Meyers. The pair welcomed daughter Kelly Marie and sons Jesse, Jody, Johnny and Blake during their 41-year marriage.\n\nIn 2021, Kris, who suffered from memory loss, announced his retirement from country music. It was revealed that his son Johnny, who holds a law degree from Pepperdine University, would take over the family's business in partnership with Morris Higham Management.\n\n\"It's been amazing to dig into my dad's catalog and history with this seasoned group of professionals ... I can't imagine a better partnership to bring the full depth of his songwriting to a new generation,\" Johnny said in a press release obtained by PEOPLE. \"The name has always been synonymous with songwriting as an art, and we're excited to reintroduce his work to new and old fans alike.\"\n\nKris was surrounded by family when he died at his home in Maui on Sept. 28, a representative for the country star told PEOPLE.\n\nHis family also shared a statement, saying, \"It is with a heavy heart that we share the news our husband/father/grandfather, Kris Kristofferson, passed away peacefully on Saturday, September 28 at home. We're all so blessed for our time with him. Thank you for loving him all these many years, and when you see a rainbow, know he's smiling down at us all.\"\n\